WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:04.250
Casting is a key ingredient in the secret
sauce of great filmmaking.

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:08.120
In the best cases, a certain performer filling
a certain character's shoes can turn a part

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.990
into a franchise-leading phenomenon.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:14.839
But the real magic is in synergy, when several
actors click; there's no X-Files without David

00:00:14.839 --> 00:00:18.590
Duchovny and Gillian Anderson, and what would
the original Star Wars movies have been without

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:21.330
Mark Hamill, Carrie Fisher, and Harrison Ford
together?

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.010
But sometimes an actor's got to go.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:26.500
It's awful for the would-be star who watches
the role end up becoming part of a massive

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.760
hit while their replacement reaps the rewards
— and it's just as bad for the actors who

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:34.290
willfully walk away from the role of a lifetime,
never to be heard from again.

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:38.579
The almost King of Gondor
The Lord of the Rings is a sprawling epic

00:00:38.579 --> 00:00:40.370
with no single lead character.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:43.980
The entire point of the film trilogy is that
it takes the combined strength and skill of

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:46.270
many to overcome the Dark Lord Sauron.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:50.110
That said, there's one character that stands
out as the film's mightiest hero, a great

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:53.960
warrior who also just so happens to be the
heir to the most powerful kingdom in Middle-earth:

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:56.400
Aragorn, son of Arathorn.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.330
It's the type of role that can turn an unknown
into a worldwide superstar — and it did

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:02.160
just that for Viggo Mortensen.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.260
Which is all too bad for Stuart Townsend,
who will always be remembered as the man who

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:08.860
almost played Aragorn – if he's remembered
at all.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:12.580
Townsend was director Peter Jackson's original
choice to play the man who would be King of

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.510
Gondor, but he was let go only a few days
into filming.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:19.300
According to Jackson, Townsend was simply
too young to be playing the veteran warrior.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.890
To this day, Mortensen is synonymous with
the character.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.060
As for poor Townsend?

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:27.080
He's gotten parts here and there, but otherwise,
he's just another casualty of the War of the

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:28.140
Ring.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:32.250
The dragons' other mother
It's become one of the biggest and most influential

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:35.860
series on television, but Game of Thrones
wasn't always a sure thing.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:39.720
To try to bring the books to the screen, HBO
ordered a pilot episode before the rest of

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.050
the series was shot — and it was a disaster.

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:44.830
Fortunately, HBO chose to stick with the project.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:48.830
Old scenes were cut, new scenes were written,
the director was replaced, and several cast

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:50.030
members were swapped out.

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:54.470
Of the latter, none were more significant
than the recasting of Daenerys Targaryen,

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:57.040
one of the most important characters in the
entire story.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.250
Tamzin Merchant played the role in the pilot.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:03.500
For undisclosed reasons, however, Emilia Clarke
was brought onboard to take her place.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:07.780
Game of Thrones has gone on to become HBO's
most successful series, and Clarke has taken

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:12.140
on starring roles in everything from romantic
comedies to Star Wars, even as she continues

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:13.850
to portray the mother of dragons.

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:17.200
Merchant, meanwhile, has continued to work
steadily, but is still waiting for her big

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.380
breakout role.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:24.010
"I am Daenerys Stormborn of House Targaryen."

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:28.010
Messing with the timeline
Back to the Future was always a zany concept:

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:32.531
a time-traveling DeLorean unites an '80s teen
with his teenage parents in the 1950s, and

00:02:32.531 --> 00:02:33.840
shenanigans ensue.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.790
It went on to become a defining movie of the
decade, and turned lead actor Michael J. Fox

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:41.920
into a superstar — but Fox almost wasn't
in the timeline at all, since he wasn't the

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:43.090
original Marty McFly.

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:46.910
In fact, Eric Stoltz had already shot weeks'
worth of footage in the role before being

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:48.420
let go by the director.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:52.570
Fox rocketed to household name status, while
Stoltz settled into steady work on TV and

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:53.590
in indie films.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:58.070
He did get a Golden Globe nomination in 1985
for Mask, but for all that talent, he never

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.610
had the star power of a time-traveling DeLorean.

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:01.610
True of us all.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:04.310
"I guess you guys aren't ready for that yet."

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:08.569
Mission impossible for this mutant
X-Men launched the modern wave of superhero

00:03:08.569 --> 00:03:10.500
movies when it was released in 2000.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:14.500
And while there are quite a few of the titular
heroes represented in that first movie, none

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.920
was more popular and more enduring than Wolverine.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:20.830
The cigar-chomping Canadian has always been
a comic book favorite, so it was absolutely

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:23.730
essential that the character be cast with
the right actor.

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:25.819
That's why the filmmakers went with Dougray
Scott.

00:03:25.819 --> 00:03:29.590
The Scottish actor was an unknown at the time,
but since the whole X-Men film was being cast

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:33.200
with relative newcomers, he seemed like a
great choice to bring the gruff living weapon

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.330
with the adamantium skeleton to life.

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:38.450
The only problem was the film that got him
attention in the first place — Mission:

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:39.560
Impossible 2.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:43.610
The film reportedly ran over schedule, forcing
Scott to stay behind on that project.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:47.390
Hugh Jackman was cast instead — the start
of what would be a long and successful career

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:49.200
in and out of superhero movies.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.200
Scott, meanwhile, has never achieved the same
level of fame.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.750
What a couple of claws might have done for
him, we'll never know.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.740
"It's part of my past, I never really, you
know…

00:03:57.740 --> 00:04:00.600
I never really think about it to be honest
with you."

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:04.360
Blown away by Arnold
When James Cameron set out to write and direct

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.580
the first Terminator film, he was a nobody.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:10.599
His biggest directorial effort up to that
time was Piranha II, a movie he was fired

00:04:10.599 --> 00:04:12.850
from which featured actor Lance Henriksen.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:16.940
Cameron liked Henriksen, and envisioned him
as the titular cyborg for Terminator — but

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:21.209
then along came an Austrian bodybuilder named
Arnold Schwarzenegger, who'd just come off

00:04:21.209 --> 00:04:23.490
of playing the lead character in Conan the
Barbarian.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:27.060
With his sheer physical presence, he was the
obvious choice to play the Terminator.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:31.320
In every way, The Terminator was Schwarzenegger's
movie, and it vaulted him into the upper echelon

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:33.160
of the decade's action stars.

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:36.750
Henriksen, meanwhile, has stayed busy over
the years, albeit in the types of character

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:40.820
actor roles that don't spawn catchphrases
or multimillion-dollar sequels.

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:42.870
"I'll be back."

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:47.280
A Tarantino twist in casting
Quentin Tarantino is one of the most meticulous

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:51.430
craftsmen in the business: he writes his own
scripts, and he knows exactly how he wants

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:52.600
to shoot them.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:55.940
Tarantino knows that a scene must be tuned
with perfect precision, and that includes

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.220
perfect casting.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:01.680
Michael Madsen turned in a memorable performance
as Mr. Blonde in Tarantino's film Reservoir

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:06.280
Dogs, so when he began filling out the roster
for his follow-up feature Pulp Fiction, Tarantino

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.850
wanted Madsen back.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:11.350
Madsen was forced to turn down the role in
favor of a part in Kevin Costner's Western

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:12.350
Wyatt Earp.

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:16.520
It probably made sense at the time: Costner
was an established star, whereas Tarantino

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:18.070
was still an indie filmmaker.

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:21.210
In Madsen's place, John Travolta was cast
as Vincent Vega.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:25.470
It was exactly what Travolta needed: he earned
an Oscar nomination and a second wind for

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:26.470
his career.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:28.320
Wyatt Earp, meanwhile, went nowhere.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:31.810
Madsen has an impressive slew of credits to
his name, but has never attracted the type

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:35.330
of fame or acclaim Travolta enjoyed post-Pulp.

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:39.290
Transforming lead actress
Megan Fox was still largely unknown when she

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:43.790
was cast in the lead female role in Michael
Bay's 2007 film Transformers.

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:47.260
The film was a huge box office hit, and Fox
became a worldwide star.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:51.900
Her return in the 2009 sequel, Transformers:
Revenge of the Fallen, cemented her status

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:54.610
as one of blockbuster cinema's hottest new
stars.

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:56.260
There was nowhere for her to go but up.

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:58.229
Until it all came crashing down.

00:05:58.229 --> 00:06:02.210
Fox was unceremoniously fired from the third
film, Transformers: Dark of the Moon.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:06.120
Initially intended to return, she was thrown
out for being too difficult to work with,

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:07.870
and for her criticism of Bay.

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:11.229
While new lead actress technically took on
a brand new character, this was still the

00:06:11.229 --> 00:06:14.540
girlfriend of Shia LaBeouf's hero — effectively
the same role.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.639
Fox's career has never been quite the same
since.

00:06:16.639 --> 00:06:20.570
Her most high-profile outings have been in
the rebooted Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:25.650
series and the ill-fated Jonah Hex; otherwise,
she hasn't seen many starring roles in films,

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:27.130
blockbuster or otherwise.

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:31.180
Sometimes, it isn't just being replaced that
damages your career, it's the reasons why.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:33.820
"You know, I tell it like it is."

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:35.530
That's a negative, Ghost rider!

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:39.229
Matthew Modine's movie career was just heating
up in the early 1980s.

00:06:39.229 --> 00:06:43.760
He seemed like a great candidate to star in
a new patriotic action movie titled Top Gun,

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:47.490
but Modine chose to walk away from the offer,
since he was uncomfortable with what he felt

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:50.050
was an unabashedly pro-military film.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:54.009
Instead, the job went to Tom Cruise, who used
his performance as Maverick to help launch

00:06:54.009 --> 00:06:56.650
one of the most successful movie careers in
history.

00:06:56.650 --> 00:07:00.600
Cruise became one of the industry's biggest
stars, and Top Gun was the turning point — the

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.820
movie that changed his life forever.

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:04.139
Modine hasn't had the same luck.

00:07:04.139 --> 00:07:08.020
He's carved out an impressive career in his
own right, turning in acclaimed performances

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:12.639
in a long list of projects that includes Full
Metal Jacket and the hit Netflix series Stranger

00:07:12.639 --> 00:07:16.520
Things, but he's kept a much lower profile
than he might have if he'd taken that fateful

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:17.520
role.

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:19.889
He refused Top Gun out of principle, but it
didn't come without cost.

00:07:19.889 --> 00:07:21.639
What a very maverick thing to do.

00:07:21.639 --> 00:07:22.639
Thanks for watching!

00:07:22.639 --> 00:07:24.960
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:26.770
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

